and shared system sections. - **Model Editing**: The chatbot identity requires explicit capability grants to modify the control-plane model selection (`model_registry` / `\n<truncated 6212 bytes>\n───┬────────────────┘ │ ▼ During Provisioning ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │ CORE INFRASTRUCTURE TIER │ │ │ │ ┌─────────────────────────┐ ┌──────────────────────┐ │ │ │ QDRANT CLUSTER │ │ STORAGE BUCKET │ │ <-- Co-located on the private │ │ (Shared Vector Brain) │ │ (Base Images & Cozo) │ │ infrastructure network │ │ :6333 / …\r\n426:L418 [A] 2026-10-26T15:26:54 **The blob gets connected to FUSE under the substrate of the local connection, and the node feeds the door.** ### The Exact Flow ``` [ BOTTOM: The Sealed Blob ] │ ▼ Substrate of the local connection (Unix Socket / SHM) [ FUSE Engine (3tchedFS) ] │ ▼ Projected upwards into local files (/run/opdbus/lungs) [ THE NODE (FUSE Side) ] │ ▼ Feeds outward [ THE DOOR (:8090) ] │ ▼ [ The External Universe ] ``` 1. **Blob $\\rightarrow$ FUSE (The Local Substrate)**: The sealed blob down at the bottom connects directly into FUSE via the local substrate (the shared memory `/dev/shm` and the local Unix domain socket). It projects the typed virtual filesystem into the node. 2. **Node $\\rightarrow$ Door (Feeding Outward)**: The node, living on the FUSE side at the top, feeds its requests, capabilities, and e …\r\n430:L422 [A] 2026-10-26T15:29:00 **Yes, exactly.** Locally, the **blobs and the spine are always connected through a local connection** (the local D-Bus bus and shared memory `/dev/shm`). * That link never crosses a network interface. * It never touches TCP or HTTP. * It is a permanent, in-memory physical connection on the host: the spine reads the sealed blobs and SHM state directly over the local bus. The node, by contrast, sits on the other side of the boundary and can only reach in by **feeding the Door (`:8090`)**.\r\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
