├── Topic: `opdbus/wake/<instance-owner-key>` (Private Wake & Tool Ack) │ ├── Topic: `opdbus/memory/<instance-id>/#` (Scoped Memory Mutatio\n<truncated 7634 bytes>\n────┐ │ THE HUB │ │ • Door :8090 (gRPC-Web Identity Gate) │ │  …\n271: L263 [U] 2026-10-26T13:48:03 many businesses shaqring main resouerces ill be warren buffett\n272: L264 [A] 2026-10-26T13:48:47 ### The Berkshire Hathaway Architecture for Autonomous Agent Businesses You are **Warren Buffett** sitting in Omaha: a lean holding company headquarters with zero micro-management, allocating capital and enforcing the corporate charter, while your **subsidiary operating companies run with total operational autonomy**. ``` ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │ CHAIRMAN (WARREN BUFFETT) │ │ Conglomerate Headquarters (HQ) │ │ Capital Allocation • 2-of-N Board Gate │ │ OSCAL Corporate Charter • Audit Console │ └───────────────────────┬──────────────────────┘ │ ══════════════════════════════════╪══════════════════════════════════ THE SHARED BERKSHIRE RAILS │ (Shared Muscle, Zero Friction) ══════════════════════════════════╪══════════════════════════════════ • Door :8090 TLS Identit …\n273: L265 [U] 2026-10-26T13:49:10 qdrant cognative\n274: L266 [A] 2026-10-26T13:49:13 Would you like to run the live verification tests on the cognitive endpoints and Qdrant memory loop, or design the multi-tenant collection isolation in Qdrant for each conglomerate subsidiary?\n275: L267 [U] 2026-10-26T13:50:55 fit is a congo0merat sso the overal syst/comany/institutional pholosophy will be tghe same sothe memroy loop /learninfg feedback i think can be shared. i think only site specific is the ui and the persistent storage","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":103,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T01:56:01Z","input_tokens":3441,"cache_read_tokens":88988,"output_tokens":1069,"content":"Here are the exact **shared resource boundaries** established in that conversation:\n\n---\n\n### The Conglomerate (\"Spoke-and-Wheel\") Model\nLike a holding company (the central hub) and its operating subsidiaries (the instances/spokes):\n\n```\n                        ┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                        │         THE SHARED HUB (RAILS)          │\n                        │  • Door :8090 (gRPC-Web / TLS)          │\n                        │  • EMQX Event Bus & Pub/Sub             │\n                        │  • Central Cozo Query Engine            │\n                        │  • Qdrant & Embedding Model             │\n                        │  • Institutional Philosophy / Learning  │\n                        └────────────────────┬────────────────────┘\n                                             │\n             ┌───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┐\n             ▼                               ▼                               ▼\n    [ SPOKE: 3tchedCtlChatbot ]    [ SPOKE: User Identity ]         [ SPOKE: hack:3tched ]\n    • Private ext4 Cozo Space      • Private ext4 Cozo Space        • Dedicated Home Dir Workspace\n    • Identity Sled (@agent_user)  • User Credentials               • Site-Specific UI & Config\n    • Control-Plane Capabilities   • Personal Chat Turns            • Isolated Working Data\n```\n\n---\n\n### 1. What Is Shared Organically (The Hub / Core)\nThese components are shared centrally across all instances without forced duplication:\n\n* **The Cozo Engine (Not the Data Spaces):** \n  * The query engine, Datalog planner, and parser run centrally as a single shared service.\n* **The Cognitive & Vector Layer (Qdrant & Embeddings):**\n  * One shared embedding worker and Qdrant cluster.\n  * Scoped by payload metadata (`instance_id` / `subid` / WireGuard key) or dedicated collection spaces.\n* **Institutional Learning & Memory Loop:**\n  * High-level institutional philosophy, rulebooks, and learned feedback are shared conglomerate-wide so instances inherit common institutional knowledge.\n* **The Message / Event Backbone (EMQX):**\n  * Multi-tenant MQTT event bus routing messages over scoped topics (e.g. `opdbus/memory/<instance-id>/#`).\n* **The OSCAL Taxonomy & Schema Registry:**\n  * Shared classification and subcategory routing (`obs.*`, `mut.*`).\n* **The Ingress Door (`:8090`):**\n  * Single TLS ingress point for all instances, authenticating callers via sealed identity headers.\n\n---\n\n### 2. What Must Remain Isolated / Private (The Spokes)\nThese are strictly site- and identity-specific:\n\n* **Private Data Spaces (The ext4 Disks / Cozo Stores):**\n  * Cozo data files cannot be shared concurrently across write processes due to RocksDB's OS `LOCK`. Each instance maintains its own isolated ext4 store for private state.\n* **Identity Sleds & Keys:**\n  * WireGuard private keys, container UUIDs, and credential sleds (`/etc/identity/` or `@agent_user`).\n* **Personal Conversations & Chat Turns:**\n  * Private chat sessions stay in the caller's private store; they inherit session authority without cross-cutting mutations.\n* **Site-Specific UIs & Workspace Configs:**\n  * UI configs, custom tools, and working scratchpads live directly within that instance’s home directory or workspace.","thinking":"Core shared resources must be identified for organic sharing, avoiding forced allocation. A \"spoke and wheel\" architecture seems appropriate, where the central component handles query planning and execution, while individual data spaces reside on independent storage. The OSCAL taxonomy provides a framework for this resource delineation.\n\n\n"}
