nd(\"x-oscal-subid\" = \"obs.standard.oscal-subid-registry.uuid@v1\"),\n190:         example = example_uuid()\n191:     )]\n192:     pub uuid: String,\n193: \n194:     /// Human-readable operational taxonomy key. Format: <category>.<component-type>.<subject>.<verb>\\[.<facet>\\]\\[@vN\\]. Immutable per subject.\n195:     #[schemars(\n196:         pattern(r\"^(src|prj|sch|mut|obs|evt|exp)\\.(this-system|system|interconnection|software|hardware|service|policy|physical|process-procedure|plan|guidance|standard|validation|network)\\.[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*\\.[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*(?:\\.[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*){0,2}(?:@v[1-9][0-9]*)?$\"),\n197:         extend(\"x-oscal-subid\" = \"sch.standard.oscal-subid-registry.subid@v1\"),\n198:         example = example_subid()\n199:     )]\n200:     pub subid: String,"}
{"step_index":118,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T01:59:06Z","input_tokens":2202,"cache_read_tokens":99980,"output_tokens":1317,"content":"Adding `subsidiary` to the taxonomy aligns directly with the conglomerate / hub-and-spoke architecture.\n\nIn the subid standard (`<category>.<component-type>.<subject>.<verb>[.<facet>][@vN]`), the component-type (2nd segment) is where high-level classification belongs.\n\n---\n\n### How It Fits into the Taxonomy\n\n```\n                   ┌─ Category: mut | obs | evt | sch | src | prj | exp\n                   │\n                   │   ┌─ High-Level Component Type: subsidiary\n                   │   │\n                   ▼   ▼\n                  mut.subsidiary.hack3tched.provision@v1\n                  obs.subsidiary.hack3tched.health@v1\n                  evt.subsidiary.hack3tched.turn-completed@v1\n                  sch.subsidiary.hack3tched.config@v1\n                                 ▲        ▲\n                                 │        └─ Action / Verb\n                                 └─ Subsidiary Subject (e.g. hack3tched, id-1)\n```\n\n---\n\n### Proposed Implementation Plan\n\n#### 1. Add `subsidiary` to Internal Categories\nIn [`crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/common/oscal.rs`](file:///srv/git/odbus-verified/crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/common/oscal.rs):\n* Add `\"subsidiary\"` to [`INTERNAL_CATEGORIES`](file:///srv/git/odbus-verified/crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/common/oscal.rs#L45-L53):\n  ```rust\n  pub const INTERNAL_CATEGORIES: &[&str] = &[\n      \"agent\",      // persona\n      \"container\",  // oci\n      \"data\",       // cozo\n      \"privacy\",    // privacy\n      \"security\",   // fail2ban\n      \"storage\",    // btrfs\n      \"subsidiary\", // conglomerate operating entities / tenant instances\n  ];\n  ```\n\n#### 2. Establish the OSCAL Standard Canonical Alias\nIn OSCAL, an autonomous operating subsidiary maps to an independent interconnected system:\n* In [`CATEGORY_ALIASES`](file:///srv/git/odbus-verified/crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/common/oscal.rs#L64-L72):\n  ```rust\n  (\"subsidiary\", \"system\"), // or \"interconnection\"\n  ```\n  * At runtime and in dashboards, it displays as `subsidiary`.\n  * When exporting standard OSCAL compliance documents (NIST 800-53 / FedRAMP), it maps cleanly to `system`.\n\n#### 3. Update the Registry Validator Pattern\nBecause [`subid_regex()`](file:///srv/git/odbus-verified/crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/common/oscal.rs#L109-L120) dynamically generates its regex pattern from `component_types()`, adding `\"subsidiary\"` to `INTERNAL_CATEGORIES` immediately makes all `*.subsidiary.*` subids valid across runtime schema checks, reflection, and the `oscal_subid_registry` plugin without broken invariants.\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to make this edit to `common/oscal.rs` and verify the subid validation tests?","thinking":"Observed the `OscalComponentType` enumeration and the `INTERNAL_CATEGORIES` and `CATEGORY_ALIASES` within the relevant code. The user's request suggests a need to define a higher-level categorization or subsumption within the existing component types. Examining the available types and their relationships is the next step to address the request.\n\n\n"}
